# Optisigns Integration API Documentation

## Overview

The Optisigns integration allows Knittt users to configure displays, create dynamic content, and trigger content display based on webhook events. The integration uses the **Optisigns GraphQL API** at `https://graphql-gateway.optisigns.com`. All endpoints require authentication via JWT token.

**Base URL:** `/api/optisigns`  
**Authentication:** Bearer token in Authorization header  
**Optisigns API:** GraphQL API at `https://graphql-gateway.optisigns.com`

> **Note:** Optisigns uses GraphQL for their API. You can test queries and mutations using their GraphQL IDE at: `https://graphql-gateway.optisigns.com/graphql`

