## 1. Configuration Management

### Get Configuration
**GET** `/api/optisigns/config`

Get the current Optisigns configuration for the tenant.

**Response:**
```json
{
  "id": "uuid",
  "tenantId": "tenant123",
  "apiToken": "***xyz", 
  "apiUrl": "https://graphql-gateway.optisigns.com",
  "isActive": true,
  "lastSync": "2024-01-01T10:00:00Z",
  "syncStatus": "success",
  "syncError": null,
  "settings": {
    "autoSync": true,
    "syncInterval": 300,
    "enableWebhooks": true,
    "defaultContentDuration": 30,
    "allowCustomAssets": true
  }
}
```

### Update Configuration
**PUT** `/api/optisigns/config`

Update Optisigns API configuration.

**Request Body:**
```json
{
  "apiToken": "your-optisigns-api-token",
  "settings": {
    "autoSync": true,
    "syncInterval": 300,
    "enableWebhooks": true,
    "defaultContentDuration": 30,
    "allowCustomAssets": true
  }
}
```

> **Note:** The API URL is automatically set to the correct Optisigns GraphQL endpoint and cannot be modified.

**Response:** Updated configuration object

### Test API Connection
**POST** `/api/optisigns/config/test`

Test connectivity to Optisigns GraphQL API with provided credentials.

**Request Body:**
```json
{
  "apiToken": "your-optisigns-api-token"
}
```

**Response:**
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "displayCount": 5,
  "accountInfo": {
    "accountName": "Your Account",
    "plan": "Professional"
  }
}
```

