## 4. Webhook Rules

### List Webhook Rules
**GET** `/api/optisigns/webhook-rules`

Get paginated list of webhook rules.

**Query Parameters:**
- `page` (integer) - Page number
- `limit` (integer) - Items per page  
- `isActive` (boolean) - Filter by active status

**Response:**
```json
{
  "rules": [
    {
      "id": "uuid",
      "name": "New Lead Welcome",
      "description": "Show welcome message for new leads",
      "webhookEndpointId": "uuid",
      "conditions": {
        "triggers": [
          {
            "field": "status",
            "operator": "equals",
            "value": "new",
            "type": "string"
          }
        ],
        "operator": "and"
      },
      "actions": {
        "contentId": "uuid",
        "displayIds": ["all"],
        "duration": 30,
        "priority": "high",
        "variables": {
          "name": "lead.name",
          "company": "lead.company"
        }
      },
      "isActive": true,
      "executionCount": 25,
      "lastExecuted": "2024-01-01T09:00:00Z",
      "priority": 50
    }
  ],
  "totalCount": 5,
  "totalPages": 1,
  "currentPage": 1
}
```

### Create Webhook Rule
**POST** `/api/optisigns/webhook-rules`

Create new webhook rule for conditional content display.

**Request Body:**
```json
{
  "name": "Sale Celebration",
  "description": "Show celebration when sale closes",
  "webhookEndpointId": "uuid",
  "conditions": {
    "triggers": [
      {
        "field": "event_type",
        "operator": "equals", 
        "value": "sale_closed",
        "type": "string"
      },
      {
        "field": "amount",
        "operator": "greater_than",
        "value": "1000",
        "type": "number"
      }
    ],
    "operator": "and"
  },
  "actions": {
    "contentId": "uuid",
    "displayIds": ["uuid1", "uuid2"],
    "duration": 45,
    "priority": "high",
    "variables": {
      "salesperson": "data.salesperson",
      "amount": "data.amount",
      "client": "data.client_name"
    }
  },
  "priority": 10
}
```

### Update Webhook Rule
**PUT** `/api/optisigns/webhook-rules/{id}`

Update existing webhook rule.

### Delete Webhook Rule
**DELETE** `/api/optisigns/webhook-rules/{id}`

Delete webhook rule.

### Test Webhook Rule
**POST** `/api/optisigns/webhook-rules/{id}/test`

Test webhook rule against sample data.

**Request Body:**
```json
{
  "sampleData": {
    "event_type": "sale_closed",
    "amount": 5000,
    "salesperson": "John Smith",
    "client_name": "Acme Corp"
  }
}
```

**Response:**
```json
{
  "matches": true,
  "variables": {
    "salesperson": "John Smith",
    "amount": 5000,
    "client": "Acme Corp",
    "timestamp": "2024-01-01T10:00:00Z"
  },
  "rule": {
    "id": "uuid",
    "name": "Sale Celebration",
    "conditions": {...},
    "actions": {...}
  }
}
```

