## Webhook Rule Condition Operators

When creating webhook rules, these operators are available:

- `equals` - Exact match
- `not_equals` - Not equal to
- `contains` - String contains value
- `not_contains` - String does not contain value
- `greater_than` - Numeric greater than
- `less_than` - Numeric less than
- `exists` - Field exists and is not null
- `not_exists` - Field does not exist or is null
- `regex` - Regular expression match

## Content Template Structure

Content templates use this structure:

```json
{
  "background": {
    "type": "color|image|video",
    "value": "#ffffff|url"
  },
  "elements": [
    {
      "type": "text|image|video|confetti|frame",
      "content": "Text content or {{variable}}",
      "position": {"x": 100, "y": 100},
      "size": {"width": 200, "height": 50},
      "style": {
        "fontSize": "24px",
        "color": "#000",
        "fontFamily": "Arial"
      }
    }
  ],
  "animations": [
    {
      "element": 0,
      "type": "fadeIn|slideIn|bounce|pulse|zoom",
      "duration": 1,
      "delay": 0,
      "easing": "ease-in|ease-out|ease-in-out"
    }
  ],
  "duration": 30,
  "transitions": []
}
```